{
	"duration": 44.104,
	"scenes": [
		{
			"id": "s1",
			"start": 0,
			"end": 5.53,
			"text": "When you send on Aztec, the private part of the work happens on your computer, not on the network."
		},
		{
			"id": "s2",
			"start": 5.53,
			"end": 13.287,
			"text": "Nulo runs it right here, with your keys and your notes. Your keys, and what is in your notes, stay on your computer."
		},
		{
			"id": "s3",
			"start": 13.287,
			"end": 19.896,
			"text": "Then your computer builds a proof: math that shows this private part follows the rules, without showing what is in it."
		},
		{
			"id": "s4",
			"start": 19.896,
			"end": 30.678,
			"text": "The proof goes to the network, with sealed notes for the people you pay. The network checks the proof, and if it holds, the transaction joins a block. It never needed your private data to trust it."
		},
		{
			"id": "s5",
			"start": 30.678,
			"end": 35.826,
			"text": "Anything a transaction does in public, the network runs in the open, for everyone to see."
		},
		{ "id": "s6", "start": 35.826, "end": 39.93, "text": "Later, one proof for a whole batch of blocks is checked on Ethereum." },
		{ "id": "s7", "start": 39.93, "end": 44.104, "text": "Building a proof takes real work, so it is the slow step before sending." }
	],
